// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`CLI help interface for 'config-manager pull cimd-profiles' should be expected english 1`] = `
"Usage: frodo config-manager pull cimd-profiles [options] [host] [realm] [username] [password]

[Experimental] Export the CIMD profiles (the allow-list of client ID URL
patterns for OAuth 2.0 clients that identify themselves with a Client ID
Metadata Document) of all realms or of one realm to
realms/<realm>/realm-config/agents/CIMDProfile/<name>.json, one file for each.
The object is written as the server lists it, without its revision; it contains
no secrets. A realm or a deployment that does not offer CIMD profiles has
nothing to export, which is not an error.

Arguments:
  host               AM base URL, e.g.: https://cdk.iam.example.com/am. To use a
                     connection profile, just specify a unique substring or
                     alias.
  realm              Realm. Specify realm as '/' for the root realm or 'realm'
                     or '/parent/child' otherwise. (default: "alpha" for
                     Identity Cloud tenants, "/" otherwise.)
  username           Username to login with. Must be an admin user with
                     appropriate rights to manage authentication journeys/trees.
                     If given without a password, and it matches the username
                     already stored in the connection profile for the target
                     host, frodo uses that profile's stored password instead of
                     requiring it on the command line.
  password           Password.

Options:
  --allow-failures   Report operations that fail, but still exit with code 0.
                     Without this option the command runs every operation,
                     prints a summary of what failed and exits with code 1.
  -f, --file <file>  A JSON file with overrides for values that differ between
                     environments, e.g. "cimd-profiles.json".
  -n, --name <name>  CIMD profile name. If specified, pulls only the profile
                     with the given name. Needs a single realm.
  -h, --help         Help
  -hh, --help-more   Help with all options.
  -hhh, --help-all   Help with all options, environment variables, and usage
                     examples.
"
`;
